From e3aea94353f71b498972d3c5fa106a6b2e6197a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:08:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Official collector: queue the night credit capture early
 (18:05/20:05 Taipei) and wait until 22:31

GitHub delays this repo's scheduled runs by 1.5-6 hours: after the 11/06
evening the runs started at 23:59, 04:33, 04:49, 05:01 and 09:19 Taipei, so
none of the 22:40/23:10/23:35 schedules captured credit statistics inside the
Site's 22:30-23:59 window.

- New daily schedules at 18:05 and 20:05 Taipei. A small wait-night job
  sleeps until 22:31 Taipei (at most 330 minutes; no wait if already past
  22:31 or if 22:31 is further away), then the usual collect-publish job runs
  and, being inside the window, includes credit statistics.
- Manual runs can do the same with the new input night=true.
- The wait job holds no concurrency slot; the collect job keeps the
  official-collector queue (moved from workflow level to job level), so other
  runs are not blocked while a night run waits.
- Weekend nights run too: if Friday night is missed, Saturday night captures
  Friday's statistics under the same Site rule.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
